# Implementation Plan — FinanceFlow AI (Agentic Financial Operations Platform)

FinanceFlow AI is an Agentic AI-powered financial operations platform built with React, Node.js + Express, MySQL, and Groq API. It automates payment reconciliation, repayment risk assessment, collection follow-ups, document intelligence, and financial analytics through controlled backend tool calling and a strict **Human-in-the-Loop** architecture.

---

## Technical & Architectural Principles

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Human-in-the-Loop Financial Rule**: The AI Agent layer **NEVER** creates official ledger allocations directly into `payment_allocations` or updates financial balances autonomously.
> The AI investigates data via tool calling, creates a candidate match in `ai_recommendations` under a `reconciliation_cases` container, and calculates a confidence score.
> **Only after an authorized user (Accountant/Manager/Admin) reviews and clicks [Approve]** does the backend execute an ACID transaction to create the `payment_allocations` record, update the `repayment_schedules` installment, update the `payments` status, and log the action in `audit_logs`.

> [!NOTE]
> **Decoupled Payment Ingestion**: Bank payments arrive without contextual entity keys (`company_id`, `loan_id`). They are ingested into `payments` as `unmatched` with source metadata. The payment lifecycle explicitly follows:
> `BANK / API PAYMENT` ➔ `payments (UNMATCHED)` ➔ `DUPLICATE CHECK` ➔ `reconciliation_cases` ➔ `AI AGENT TOOL CALLING` ➔ `ai_recommendations` ➔ `HUMAN VERIFICATION (Approve/Reject/Pending)` ➔ `payment_allocations` ➔ `repayment_schedules UPDATE` ➔ `audit_logs`.

> [!TIP]
> **Learnable Code & Mandatory Documentation**: Every function will feature standardized data-flow top comments (Purpose, Called by, Receives, Data source, Returns, Calls, Error handling), every React component will document props, and every module/table/page will have a dedicated `.md` file with a **Mentor Questions** section.

