## 3. Business Rules Engine

| Rule ID | Business Requirement | Technical Implementation |
|---|---|---|
| **BR-01** | One payment split across multiple installments | Supported via multiple `payment_allocations` rows pointing to different `repayment_schedules` rows. |
| **BR-02** | Multiple payments for one installment | Supported via multiple `payment_allocations` rows linking different payments to the same `repayment_schedules.id`. |
| **BR-03** | Overpayment handling | If `amount > total_due`, allocate `total_due` to installment and set `allocation_type='overpayment'` for excess. Flag for accountant review. |
| **BR-04** | AI Confidence Score $\ge 90\%$ | Strong Recommendation. Auto-populated for quick 1-click confirmation. |
| **BR-05** | AI Confidence Score $70\% - 89\%$ | Medium Confidence. Detailed review required by accountant before approval. |
| **BR-06** | AI Confidence Score $< 70\%$ | Low Confidence. Recommendation flagged, system prompts manual investigation. |
| **BR-07** | Similar Company Names | Agent evaluates multiple signals: Sender Name + Bank Account Number + Transaction Reference + Installment Amount. |
| **BR-08** | Role-Based Access Control (RBAC) | `Admin`, `Manager`, `Accountant` can approve/reject. `Viewer` is read-only. |
| **BR-09** | Accountant Manual Override | Accountant can reject AI recommendation and manually select company/loan with a mandatory `override_reason` logged in audit trail. |
| **BR-10** | Duplicate Bank Transactions | Unique constraint on `transaction_reference` + composite pattern check on `sender` + `amount` + `date` + `bank_reference`. |

